    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0630" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg624"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Goschen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The U. S. commissioner on the Samoan land
                    commission reports, under date of September 12, 1894, that the labors of the
                    commissioners can easily be concluded within sixty days from that date, and that
                    there is no necessity for the commissioners remaining in Samoa longer than the
                    actual investigations of the claims may <pb facs="0631" n="625" xml:id="pg625"/>
                    require, only the services of the secretary being needed to prepare the schedule
                    of papers for final delivery to the supreme court.</p>
                <p>In view of this statement I have the honor to suggest that the three Governments
                    cable identic instructions to their respective commissioners that the work must
                    be completed so that the labors of the commission shall end and all reports and
                    papers shall be forwarded to the supreme court within the time now agreed on,
                    viz, December 31, 1894.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
